i sold an nft of my meme for  600 000 and this is that story my name  is chris torres but you may know me as  the creator of nancat  so this all started around the year 2010  one day i was walking through a pet  store and i just saw this beautiful  russian blue kitten  and you know i just decided to take him  it was just so cute to not adopt  and i named him marty and he was my baby  he was always there for me he was the  craziest  most fastest cat ever he was just always  running around the house  and actually he would just kind of roam  the neighborhood he was always on an  adventure of some sort  such a beautiful soul of a cat he was  such a great cat  and i ended up incorporating marty into  a lot of my comics i've been drawing  comics for a long time now called lol  comics and he just kind of became a  featured character in my series  so around 2011 a lot of natural  disasters were happening around the  world a lot of typhoons a lot of  earthquakes  and i saw a lot of artists actually  begin to do like donation drives for the  american red cross  doctors without borders and a few other  charities and then um i decided to join  in  at the time i didn't really have much of  a following but i would just  hop on to live stream at least once a  day so now i'd be like hey everybody  what do you want me to draw one day it  was just kind of slow nobody was really  in there so i kind of asked everybody  involved um you know what do you guys  want to see  and all the words you know all the  keywords started popping up i saw cat  i saw rainbows i saw breakfast pastry  so i just started doodling what  ended up being yan cat it was just a cat  with a breakfast pastry body  and at the time the trail wasn't going  behind them it was just kind of going  all over the place  i got a like 100 tip that day and which  went straight to charity which was  awesome uh i drew it and then i went to  sleep that night i  and i just kind of dreamt a scenario  where  the doodle that i had drawn with marty  flying through space kind of was like  animated and pixelated in my head and i  just kind of woke up i remember it was  almost midnight  that night i woke up and i was like i  have to do this it's still fresh in my  mind  so i you know i ran downstairs and i  began drawing and it took about  it took about six hours i know i know  the sun was coming up by the time i  finished  so i posted it on tumblr and uh  overnight it had thousands of notes and  it's just lots of messages of people  just saying how much they loved it a few  days passed and then it ended up being  on youtube  the user sarah june actually uploaded  nyanka with the  popular song from danielle called you  know the nyani and yanian song  and that's where it really just like  exploded into the mainstream  lots of people were inspired by mancat  and ended up being this huge global  phenomenon  i did show marty the animation he was  very cat-like in his response where he  just didn't care  i want to say around january of 2021  this year  i had a good friend of mine named lizzie  she actually contacted me and was like  look all these people  are creating artwork in the nft market  making not only money but making  themselves known  i think the easiest way to uh explain  nfts  it's like a digital signature that can't  be replicated it ties  the artwork to you everybody will know  on the blockchain  that this artist created this artwork  there's nobody that can make a forgery  and get away with it the first nan cats  sold for six hundred thousand dollars i  held all the rights to the ncat and like  copyrights and the trademarks and stuff  like that  the owner of the nft itself basically  got a promise for me that this nft  will be the only one based on the  original video  ever the person that owns it now is  basically holding on to  you know basically a trading card and  from there he can sell it for  however much he or she wants in the  future if nyancat continues to be  popular in the  years to come the owner can actually  sell it for millions of dollars if they  choose to  to somebody that wants to buy it the the  best thing about it though is that  whenever somebody sells your nft  that you created you actually do get a  percentage of it uh after that i started  making  other damn cats i started collaborating  with artists in the nft space  i helped zoe sell her and of tea and  actually helped harold get his  nft set up and then after that i created  what i call the nancat  classic collection which is based off of  old nan cats that i created  back in 2011 or so and i just never  released so i've actually sold  i want to say over 700 more nfts since  the original nan cat  we're kind of in talks for a possible tv  show we're talking about possible new  games i'm very excited for the future  for it and i hope that dan cat  still has a place 10 years from now back  in 2012 marty  ended up becoming sick he ended up  having fip  and he sadly passed away that year and  it was really sad um we tried  we tried so hard to save him but there  was just nothing that really could be  done  but it's also kind of cool that his  legacy lives on  i will always look at the image of dan  cat flying around and i will always see  marty like  that is the behavior that he had just  zooming around all the time and i could  totally see him right now just in space  flying around  with just rainbows everywhere  [Music]  you
 

